From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.mediacontrol: Windows.Media.Control, the desktop's media sessions from MPRIS (9862)

GlobalSystemMediaTransportControlsSessionManager is how launchers, widgets and "now playing"
tools see and control what plays; Wox 2.5's media plugin asked for it and got "Failed to find
library". It is new: RequestAsync, GetSessions, GetCurrentSession, SessionsChanged and
CurrentSessionChanged; a session's SourceAppUserModelId, TryGetMediaPropertiesAsync (title, artist,
album, album artist, track number, cover), GetPlaybackInfo (status, controls, repeat, rate, shuffle),
GetTimelineProperties, TryPlay/Pause/Stop/TogglePlayPause/SkipNext/SkipPrevious, repeat, shuffle,
rate and position, and its three changed events.

The sessions are the MPRIS players on the user's session bus: the Linux programs' own, and every
Windows program's transport controls, which 6523 publishes there. A Windows program's session is
named by its executable (probe.exe), a Linux program's by its desktop entry. The commands are the
player's Play, Pause, PlayPause, Stop, Next, Previous, SetPosition and its LoopStatus, Shuffle and
Rate. The list is read when asked; once an event handler is added a thread looks every half second
and raises the events from there, as Windows raises them from a thread of its own. The current
session is the one that plays. Record, fast forward, rewind and the channel buttons are not in MPRIS:
false. The cover is read from a file:// art URL only. The unix side has a connection of its own,
to the user's session bus only (never one started for us), as the publishing side.
